          "buttonOnMobile": false,
          "label": "<p>A patient has only two hypopigmented, anaesthetic skin patches, but a slit-skin </p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>A patient has only two hypopigmented, anaesthetic skin patches, but a slit-skin smear from the ear lobe shows acid-fast bacilli. Which treatment regimen should be prescribed?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>PB-MDT (rifampicin + dapsone) for 6 months</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>A positive slit-skin smear automatically classifies the patient as multibacillary, regardless of how few skin lesions are present. The two-drug PB regimen would be insufficient.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>MB-MDT (rifampicin + clofazimine + dapsone) for 6 months</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>The correct three-drug combination is chosen, but the duration must be 12 months, not 6. The 6-month course applies only to PB-MDT.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>MB-MDT (rifampicin + clofazimine + dapsone) for 12 months</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. A positive slit-skin smear at any site makes the disease multibacillary regardless of lesion count, requiring the full three-drug MB-MDT regimen for 12 months.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>PB-MDT (rifampicin + dapsone) for 12 months</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>PB-MDT contains only two drugs. A smear-positive patient needs three drugs (adding clofazimine), not simply a longer duration of the two-drug regimen.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "The answer is MB-MDT for 12 months. Remember: a positive smear overrides lesion count — the patient is multibacillary and needs all three drugs (rifampicin + clofazimine + dapsone) for the full 12-month course."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Correct! The key rule: a positive slit-skin smear at any site means multibacillary disease, regardless of lesion count. This requires the full MB-MDT regimen — rifampicin, clofazimine, and dapsone — for 12 months."
                }
              ],
